    "done_when": "Each of these thirteen callers stops parsing timestamps itself and calls reckon._timestamps.parse_utc:\n- reckon/crew/hold.py:_as_moment\n- reckon/crew/lane_document.py:_parse_stamp\n- reckon/crew/lane_evidence.py:_moment\n- reckon/crew/obligations.py:_seconds_since\n- reckon/crew/pace_replay.py:_read\n- reckon/crew/paid_lanes.py:_parse_stamp\n- reckon/crew/query.py:_normalize_stamp\n- reckon/crew/resumption.py:_parse_stamp\n- reckon/crew/rollout.py:_parse_timestamp\n- reckon/crew/routing.py:_parse_utc_timestamp\n- reckon/crew/runs.py:_stream_quiet_seconds\n- reckon/crew/summary.py:_row_moment\n- reckon/crew/window_reading.py:_parse_stamp\n\nA caller whose policy differs from parse_utc's keeps that policy in a line or two around the call, never in a second parser. query.py:_normalize_stamp reports a zoneless value as unknown rather than assuming UTC, and keeps doing so. A private helper left with no caller is deleted.\n\nBefore editing, record each caller's current output at base 142cdf05 over one shared input list: an aware ISO string, a Z-suffixed string, a naive string, a date-only string, an epoch number, an empty string, None, a non-string object and garbage text. Commit that table as the expectations of tests/test_timestamp_callers_batch_a.py. The test asserts every migrated caller still produces its recorded output.\n\nA second test walks the thirteen modules with ast and asserts that no fromisoformat call remains in them.\n\nThat file, and the existing test file of each touched module that has one, pass at exit 0. The manifest records base and head arms over the same file set in the armed JSON form with their FAILED ids, and the head arm runs at the committed head. The declared negative control is applied, the recorded-output case for hold._as_moment is observed to fail, and that log's absolute path is in the manifest with an EXIT= line and the FAILED id. The full project suite is not run by this node.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
